# Data Spec: `extracted_data.json`

Every scraped episode produces one file at `data/raw/{episode_id}/extracted_data.json`.

`episode_id` format: `{series_slug}_s{season:02d}_e{episode:02d}` — e.g. `the_office_s02_e04`.

---

## Full schema

```json
{
  "episode_id": "the_office_s02_e04",

  "metadata": {
    "episode_id": "the_office_s02_e04",
    "series_title": "The Office",
    "series_slug": "the_office",
    "episode_title": "The Fire",
    "season_number": 2,
    "episode_number": 4,
    "air_date": "2006-01-19",
    "provenance": {
      "source": "fandom_wiki",
      "wiki_page_title": "The_Fire",
      "wiki_origin": "https://theoffice.fandom.com",
      "wiki_api_url": "https://theoffice.fandom.com/api.php?action=parse&page=The_Fire&..."
    }
  },

  "narrative": {
    "cold_open": "string or null",
    "synopsis": "string or null",
    "cast": {
      "main": ["Steve Carell as Michael Scott", "John Krasinski as Jim Halpert"],
      "supporting": ["..."],
      "recurring": ["..."],
      "other": []
    }
  }
}
```

---

## Field rules

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| `episode_id` (root) | Must match the directory name and `metadata.episode_id`. |
| `metadata.air_date` | ISO date string (`YYYY-MM-DD`) parsed from wiki infobox, or `null` if not found. Never a placeholder. |
| `metadata.provenance.source` | Always `"fandom_wiki"`. Not show-specific. |
| `narrative.cold_open` | Text from the `Cold_open` or `Cold_Open` section. `null` if section is absent or empty. |
| `narrative.synopsis` | Text from `Summary` section, falling back to `Synopsis` section. `null` if neither exists. |
| `narrative.cast` | Always has all four keys: `main`, `supporting`, `recurring`, `other`. Each is a list of strings (may be empty list `[]`). Each string is a full credit line, e.g. `"Steve Carell as Michael Scott"`. |

---

## What is NOT in this file

These keys existed in the old project (`sitcom-ml-project`) as transitional fields. **Do not include them:**

- `narrative.plot` — was cold_open + synopsis concatenated
- `narrative.plot_sections_used`
- `narrative.trivia`
- `narrative.cast_text_debug`
- `narrative.lede_text`
- `social` — the entire top-level key

If you see any of these in the output, it is a bug.

---

## Other files written per episode

These are cached artifacts. They are not the primary contract but must be present:

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `wiki_parse_api.json` | Raw MediaWiki parse API JSON response |
| `wiki_article_from_api.html` | Full article HTML fragment from the API |
| `wiki_extracted.json` | Parsed sections dict + infobox text + lede text |

---

## Combined episodes

When one wiki page covers two broadcast episodes (e.g. S4E01 and S4E02 both on page `Fun_Run`):
- One HTTP fetch is made
- Two directories are written: `data/raw/the_office_s04_e01/` and `data/raw/the_office_s04_e02/`
- Each gets its own `extracted_data.json` with the correct `episode_number` and `episode_id`
- `metadata.season_number` and `metadata.episode_number` are specific to each file (not shared)
- All other narrative content is duplicated (same synopsis, same cast — the wiki page covers both)
